course: dictionary
lesson: 800
title: Beetroot, a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Lunch at Granny's often starts with borshch, a red beetroot soup served with sour cream.» Here beetroot is food, because you can eat it in soup.
explain: The phrase «go as red as a beetroot» means to blush, when your face turns a deep red. Here beetroot describes a colour, not a vegetable. Ask yourself: does the word fit as food, or as a colour?
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence. A beetroot cannot blush, so the colour meaning fits a red face, and the vegetable meaning fits the soup. Good readers test both meanings before they choose.
fact: Beetroot is a round, dark red root vegetable that grows under the ground.
fact: Beetroot is also used to describe a deep red colour, especially a red face.
fact: Beetroot is eaten cooked, pickled or raw, in salads and in soup.
fact: «Borshch» is a red beetroot soup, often served with sour cream.
fact: «Beetroot can turn poo and wee pink for a day, which is harmless.»
exercise: «Lunch at Granny's often starts with borshch, a red beetroot soup.» What is a beetroot in this sentence? | *A round, dark red root vegetable | A type of sour cream | A deep red colour | A kind of spoon
exercise: «Her face went as red as a beetroot.» What does beetroot describe here? | A sort of soup | A green leafy plant | A big, round bowl | *A deep red colour, like a blush
exercise: Which of these is a root vegetable? | Lettuce | *Beetroot | Broccoli | Peas
test: Where does a beetroot grow? | On top of clouds | In the sea | *Under the ground | On tall trees
test: Ben says, «Jess went beetroot when she read her name out.» What does he mean? | *She turned a deep red colour, like a blush | She ate a beetroot | She grew a tall plant | She sang loudly
exam: Which meaning of beetroot fits «a slice of beetroot in a burger» in Australia and New Zealand? | A kind of sour cream | The colour red | A type of bread | *The vegetable
